---------------------------------------------------------------------------
II - Compile + install
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

+ Linux, *BSD, BeOS, IRIX, QNX, SunOS, AtheOS, Darwin:

	You need:
		+ GCC 2.95.x
		+ GNU make
		+ NetBSD: you also need the Pth library

	Type:
		$ sh configure 
		$ gmake (or make)
		$ su
		$ gmake install (or make install)

		and NEVER FORGET: always use GNU make 


+ AmigaOS + GeekGadgets

	AmigaOS/68k can also be cross-compiled from Linux or BSD.
	See http://www.nmo-sdk.org/amigaos/crossgcc .

	m68k:	
		You need: 
			+ GeekGadgets (with ixemul 48.x and libnix)
			+ gcc 2.95.x m68k
			+ pthread 1.3.x m68k
			+ Includes OS 3.5
	
		You have to type:
			2- sh configure
			3- make

	WarpUP: in construction !
		You need: 
			+ GeekGadgets (with ixemul 48.1 and libnix)
			+ gcc 2.95.x WarpUP
			+ pthread 1.3.x PPC
			+ Includes OS 3.5
	
		Type:
			$ sh configure --cc=ppc-amigaos-gcc --os=WarpUP
			$ make

	
+ Windows:
	You need either:
		+ Visual Studio 6 or 7 (sorry...).
		+ Borland C++ 5.5 
			(the BCC 5.5 command line tools are avaible free of charges 
			 from http://www.borland.com)

+ MacOS:
	You need CodeWarrior 5 and CarbonLib (v1.2+).


+ MacOS X:
	You need CodeWarriot 5 or the Public Beta Tools 
    (tested with the October 2000 Release)


	
Hope this helps !

nmo-sdk@nmo-sdk.org

